Fines are **off** until you turn on **Charge library fines** in Library Settings. While off, nothing
is charged and unpaid fines block nothing.

**Only students are fined.** Teachers and staff never are.

## How a fine is made

A library fine is an ordinary pending charge on the student's account. That means it appears on
their statement and is settled the way any other charge is. The library never touches your ledger
itself.

| Kind | When it is charged |
| --- | --- |
| Overdue | Once, when the book is checked in. While the book is out it is only a projection |
| Lost | When a librarian declares the book lost |
| Damage | When a librarian records damage |

Settings: **Fine per late day**, **Days late before fining starts**, **Most for one late book**
(0 for no cap), **Count school days only** (weekends, holidays and out-of-term days are not late
days), **Lost book, when no price is recorded**, **Added to every lost book**, **Stop borrowing when
owing more than** (0 means any unpaid fine blocks) and **Days to pay**.

## The Fines page

**Library → Fines** lists unpaid, paid and waived fines. Someone with **Waive unpaid library fines**
can waive an unpaid fine with a reason: it is voided without any ledger entry.

## How families pay

- At the office, through Manual Payment Entry, under the student ID.
- Online, if your school takes online payments and **Let parents pay library fines online** is on.
  Fines also appear on the online payments screens whether or not the portal library is on.

